    "---\n",
    "### Part 1  One Tree Fir\n",
    "\n",
    "A single decision tree is our **building block**. It's interpretable but unstable  resample the data slightly and the tree can change completely."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1000012",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1a. Fit a depth-4 tree and read its decision paths\n",
    "\n",
    "We use `max_depth=4` so the tree stays small enough to **print and read**  like a fraud analyst's mental checklist. We also use `class_weight=\"balanced\"`  \n",
    "because only ~8% of transactions are fraud; without it the tree would predict \"legit\" for everyone."
   ]
  },
